constexpr Box boxes[] = {
  {"LL-TB-000007", "Bear's Legacy", 33.0409968338934, -97.3783864551928, 1, 1, "Bear wasn't much to look at if you were expecting a big, fearsome animal. He was a small terrier with a big heart, a gentle spirit, and a favorite place in the world: someone's lap.\n\nHe was a house dog, obedient and content to spend his days close to the people he loved. He didn't need grand adventures or wide-open spaces. A warm home, a familiar voice, and a little affection were more than enough.\n\nBut one day, Bear slipped away from home.\n\nHe wandered near the local high school, just a block from where he lived. While standing beside the road, he was struck by a passing vehicle. The circumstances suggested it may have been intentional, though no one can say for certain.\n\nBear never made it home.\n\nIt's a heartbreaking ending for a dog who never meant anyone any harm. But his story deserves to be remembered for more than the way it ended.\n\nBear was loved. He was loyal. And for the people who knew him, the world was a little brighter because he was in it.\n\nThis treasure is dedicated to Bear and to all the companions who leave paw prints on our hearts long after they're gone.\n\nRest easy, Bear. You were a good boy.", "This treasure is located near the large community dog park in Liberty Trails. You do not need to enter the dog park to find it. Look around the area outside the dog park's fence.", "f989ec6e35690d7174f780e8d1958a46c51eae2d8cf5cb7f62d45d801ba9de14"},
  {"LL-TB-000016", "The Hidden Hedge", 33.0407989105428, -97.370252414568, 1, 1, "Not every adventure begins on a winding forest trail. Sometimes, the best little secrets are hiding just beyond your own neighborhood!\n\nDown a quiet gravel road, an old tree stands guard over a treasure waiting to be discovered. Blink, and you might walk right past it!\n\nRanger Rowan's Hint:\n\nFollow the gravel road past the pump station and keep your eyes peeled for a tree near the fence line. Your treasure is tucked away on the other side, out of plain sight.\n\nRemember, trailblazers: Only enter where access is permitted. Never climb or cross a barbed-wire fence.", "", "d8fc1fc324ab0cd0156d87d12eb1d353d12c0bddf4b86e92433f4cb303f4f253"},
  {"LL-TB-000017", "The Emerald Viper Escape", 33.0430245096367, -97.3803705017911, 1, 1, "WARNING! DANGEROUS SNAKE ON THE LOOSE!\n\nDeep in the Amazon rainforest, I discovered an incredibly rare snake known as the Amazonian Emerald Pit Viper. Its brilliant green scales make it nearly invisible among the leaves, and a single bite can be deadly!\n\nI brought it here in this very box, but something has gone terribly wrong.\n\nIT ESCAPED!\n\nI've searched everywhere, but the snake has vanished into the surrounding trees. It could be hiding beneath the leaves, curled around a branch, or watching you right now.\n\nKeep your eyes open, watch your step, and whatever you do…\n\nDON'T LET IT BITE YOU!", "", "7c14dcd855e318199f407e38baa74b53c9892c176b12a5cc901e2044a1f52867"},
  {"LL-TB-000018", "The Boy Who Never Came Back", 33.0419371690753, -97.3679227891319, 1, 1, "If you're reading this, there's still a chance.\n\nI found a strange machine beneath this bridge. I thought it was broken, but when I climbed inside, it sent me 50 years into the past. Now I'm trapped here, and I don't know how to get home.\n\nI need you to find me before I discover that machine. Find the boy I used to be, and tell him whatever he does, NEVER go inside.\n\nPlease hurry. I'm counting on you.", "Somewhere at the entrance to Lone Star", "af9ea2b90312b46a292d80de9eaf20afda70d10584cbff395759a27512e2942d"},
};
constexpr double north = 33.052, south = 33.032, west = -97.386, east = -97.362;
